17.8 Venn diagram and UpSet
The words three French artists use in their songs: a word is in an artist’s set when it appears in their lyrics. data-to-viz: no more than three sets in a Venn diagram, a number in every region - the UpSet plot handles more.

17.8.1 Two and three sets
Two artists: circle areas and the overlap proportional to the word counts. Three: the classic layout, counts and shares from a label function.
Source: R Graph Gallery - Venn diagram; data-to-viz - Venn diagram (1, 2). Data: Words in the songs of three French artists, data-to-viz example dataset 14_SeveralIndepLists (Yan Holtz); licence: MIT (data_to_viz repository).

(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange
  [{:data words :mapping {:set :artist :item :word}
    :charts [(chart/venn {:sets ["booba" "nekfeu"]})] :labels {:title "two artists"}}
   {:data words :mapping {:set :artist :item :word}
    :charts [(chart/venn {:region-labels #(format "%d\n%.0f%%" (:size %) (* 100.0 (double (:share %))))})]
    :labels {:title "three artists"}}]
  {:columns 2})
 {:width 1000 :height 480})






17.8.2 UpSet plot
Bars of the exact intersections (largest first) over a dot matrix of the sets in each: from cljplot2.data.sets/upset-rows and membership-rows.
Source: R Graph Gallery - Venn diagram (the UpSetR alternative). Data: Words in the songs of three French artists, data-to-viz example dataset 14_SeveralIndepLists (Yan Holtz); licence: MIT (data_to_viz repository).

(plot/render-image
 (let [m {:set :artist :item :word}
       dots (sets/membership-rows words m)]
   (plot/arrange [{:data (sets/upset-rows words m) :mapping {:x :combination :y :size}
                   :scales {:x {:axis false}}
                   :charts [(chart/bar {:value-label true})] :labels {:title "Words shared by the artists" :x nil :y "words"}}
                  {:data dots :mapping {:x :combination :y :set}
                   :theme {:axis {:x {:label-rotation -45}}}
                   :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 12 :color [210 210 210]})
                            (chart/scatter {:data (filter :member? dots) :size 12 :color :black})]
                   :labels {:x nil :y nil}}]
                 {:columns 1 :heights [3 2]}))
 {:width 900 :height 650})

19.8 Circular plots
Ordinary charts in polar coordinates: the angle runs along a variable, the radius along another; :start, :direction, :inner and :span shape the circle.

19.8.1 Basic, customised, part of the circle
Air passengers by month around the circle, a ring per year: the default circle, then a hole, a start at 3 o’clock counter-clockwise, and half a circle.
Source: R Graph Gallery - Basic circular plot, custom a track, part of the circular plot (1, 2, 3). Data: Monthly airline passengers, 1949-1960, R datasets package AirPassengers (Box & Jenkins 1976); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(def months ["Jan" "Feb" "Mar" "Apr" "May" "Jun" "Jul" "Aug" "Sep" "Oct" "Nov" "Dec"])


(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange (vec (for [[coord title] [[{:kind :polar} "default"]
                                         [{:kind :polar :inner 0.3 :start 90 :direction :counter-clockwise} "hole, start, direction"]
                                         [{:kind :polar :span 180 :start -90} "half a circle"]]]
                      {:data air-passengers :mapping {:x :month :y :passengers :color :year}
                       :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 5})]
                       :coord coord
                       :scales {:x {:domain months}}
                       :legend false
                       :labels {:title title :x nil :y nil}}))
               {:columns 3})
 {:width 1000 :height 400})






19.8.2 Chart types, several plots
Points, a line per year and bars of the monthly totals in the same circle, and one circular plot per period.
Source: R Graph Gallery - Plot types for circular plot, several circular plots in a figure (1, 2). Data: Monthly airline passengers, 1949-1960, R datasets package AirPassengers (Box & Jenkins 1976); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(def periods
  (mapv #(assoc % :period (cond (&lt;= (long (:year %)) 1952) "1949-1952" (&lt;= (long (:year %)) 1956) "1953-1956" :else "1957-1960"))
        air-passengers))


(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange
  [{:data air-passengers :mapping {:x :month :y :passengers}
    :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 4})] :coord {:kind :polar :inner 0.2} :scales {:x {:domain months}}
    :labels {:title "points" :x nil :y nil}}
   {:data air-passengers :mapping {:x :month :y :passengers :group :year}
    :charts [(chart/line {:sort false :color [70 130 180 150]})] :coord {:kind :polar :inner 0.2} :scales {:x {:domain months}}
    :labels {:title "a line per year" :x nil :y nil}}
   {:data air-passengers :mapping {:x :month :y :passengers}
    :charts [(chart/bar {:stat :sum})] :coord {:kind :polar :inner 0.2} :scales {:x {:domain months}}
    :labels {:title "bars: monthly totals" :x nil :y nil}}]
  {:columns 3})
 {:width 1000 :height 400})





(plot/render-image
 {:data periods :mapping {:x :month :y :passengers :group :year :facet :period}
  :charts [(chart/line {:sort false})]
  :coord {:kind :polar :inner 0.2}
  :scales {:x {:domain months}}
  :labels {:title "One circular plot per period" :x nil :y nil}}
 {:width 1000 :height 420})

21.1.1 Fig 1.1 Histograms
GCSE scores of the A-level chemistry candidates, a panel per A-level score.
Source: Lattice Fig 1.1. Data: A-level chemistry scores, England 1997, R mlmRev package Chem97 (Yang et al. 2002); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (mlmRev).

(plot/render-image
 {:data chem97
  :mapping {:x :gcsescore :facet :score}
  :charts [(chart/histogram)]
  :facets {:columns 3}
  :labels {:x "gcsescore" :y "Percent of Total"}}
 {:width 800 :height 500})






21.1.2 Fig 1.2 Densities
Source: Lattice Fig 1.2. Data: A-level chemistry scores, England 1997, R mlmRev package Chem97 (Yang et al. 2002); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (mlmRev).

(plot/render-image
 {:data chem97
  :mapping {:x :gcsescore :facet :score}
  :charts [(chart/density)]
  :facets {:columns 3}
  :labels {:x "gcsescore" :y "Density"}}
 {:width 800 :height 500})






21.1.3 Fig 1.3 Grouped densities
The six densities in one panel, coloured by score; the score is a number, declared categorical for the colours.
Source: Lattice Fig 1.3. Data: A-level chemistry scores, England 1997, R mlmRev package Chem97 (Yang et al. 2002); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (mlmRev).

(plot/render-image
 {:data chem97
  :mapping {:x :gcsescore :color :score}
  :scales {:color {:type :categorical}}
  :charts [(chart/density)]
  :labels {:x "gcsescore" :y "Density"}}
 {:width 700 :height 450})






21.1.4 Fig 1.4 Two plots on a page
Source: Lattice Fig 1.4. Data: A-level chemistry scores, England 1997, R mlmRev package Chem97 (Yang et al. 2002); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (mlmRev).

(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange [{:data chem97
                 :mapping {:x :gcsescore :facet :score}
                 :charts [(chart/histogram)]
                 :facets {:columns 2}
                 :labels {:x "gcsescore" :y "Percent of Total"}}
                {:data chem97
                 :mapping {:x :gcsescore :color :score}
                 :scales {:color {:type :categorical :title "score"}}
                 :charts [(chart/density)]
                 :labels {:x "gcsescore" :y "Density"}}]
               {:columns 1})
 {:width 600 :height 800})

21.2 Chapter 2 - A Technical Overview of lattice

21.2.1 Fig 2.1 Two conditioning variables
Oat yield by nitrogen, a panel per variety (columns) and block (rows): points joined by lines.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.1. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet-col :variety :facet-row :block}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter)]
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 700 :height 800})






21.2.2 Fig 2.2 One block
Source: Lattice Fig 2.2. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data (filterv #(= "I" (:block %)) oats)
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet :variety}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter)]
  :facets {:columns 3}
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 800 :height 450})






21.2.3 Fig 2.3 Banked to 45 degrees
Lattice’s aspect = "xy" chooses the panel shape from the slopes of the lines; here the image is narrow instead.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.3. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet-col :variety :facet-row :block}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter {:size 3})]
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 380 :height 800})






21.2.4 Fig 2.4 Eighteen panels in three rows
Source: Lattice Fig 2.4. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet #(str (:block %) " " (:variety %))}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter {:size 3})]
  :facets {:columns 6}
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 1000 :height 550})






21.2.5 Fig 2.5 Gaps between blocks
Lattice widens chosen gaps between panels (between); here each block is its own plot, arranged.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.5. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange (for [block ["I" "II" "III" "IV" "V" "VI"]]
                 {:data (filterv #(= block (:block %)) oats)
                  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet :variety}
                  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter {:size 3})]
                  :scales {:y {:domain [50 180]}}
                  :facets {:columns 3}
                  :labels {:title (str "Block " block) :x nil :y nil}})
               {:columns 2})
 {:width 1000 :height 700})






21.2.6 Fig 2.6 Dot plot
Barley yield of each variety at six sites, the two years in two shapes. Sites, varieties and years keep R’s factor order (nu/levels); lattice fills panels from the bottom, so the sites run top-down reversed.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.6. Data: Barley yields, Minnesota 1931-1932, R lattice package barley (Immer et al. 1934; Fisher 1971; Cleveland 1993); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (lattice).

(plot/render-image
 {:data barley
  :mapping {:x :yield :y :variety :shape :year :facet :site}
  :scales {:y {:domain (nu/levels :barley :variety)}
           :facet {:domain (vec (rseq (nu/levels :barley :site)))}
           :shape {:domain (nu/levels :barley :year)}}
  :charts [(chart/scatter)]
  :facets {:columns 1}
  :theme {:text {:tick-label {:size 8}}}
  :labels {:x "yield" :y nil}}
 {:width 600 :height 800})






21.2.7 Fig 2.7 Groups within panels
Source: Lattice Fig 2.7. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :shape :variety :group :variety :facet :block}
  :charts [(chart/line {:color :darkgrey}) (chart/scatter {:color :black :size 6})]
  :facets {:columns 6}
  :labels {:title "Yield of three varieties of oats - a 3 x 4 split plot experiment with 6 blocks"
           :x "Nitrogen concentration (cwt/acre)" :y "Yield (bushels/acre)"}}
 {:width 1000 :height 400})






21.2.8 Fig 2.8 Stacked bars
Titanic passengers by class, stacked by survival, a panel per age and sex.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.8. Data: Titanic passengers and crew by class, sex, age and survival, R datasets package Titanic (Dawson 1995); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(def titanic-panels ["Child Male" "Child Female" "Adult Male" "Adult Female"])


(plot/render-image
 {:data titanic
  :mapping {:x :n :y :class :color :survived :facet #(str (:age %) " " (:sex %))}
  :scales {:facet {:domain titanic-panels}}
  :charts [(chart/bar {:position :stack})]
  :facets {:columns 4}
  :theme {:panel {:grid {:x :none :y :none}}}
  :labels {:x "Freq" :y nil}}
 {:width 900 :height 350})






21.2.9 Fig 2.9 Free scales
Each panel its own count axis, so the small groups are readable.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.9. Data: Titanic passengers and crew by class, sex, age and survival, R datasets package Titanic (Dawson 1995); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 {:data titanic
  :mapping {:x :n :y :class :color :survived :facet #(str (:age %) " " (:sex %))}
  :scales {:facet {:domain titanic-panels}}
  :charts [(chart/bar {:position :stack})]
  :facets {:columns 4 :scales {:x :free}}
  :theme {:panel {:grid {:x :none :y :none}}}
  :labels {:x "Freq" :y nil}}
 {:width 900 :height 350})






21.2.10 Fig 2.10 Vertical grid lines
Source: Lattice Fig 2.10. Data: Titanic passengers and crew by class, sex, age and survival, R datasets package Titanic (Dawson 1995); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 {:data titanic
  :mapping {:x :n :y :class :color :survived :facet #(str (:age %) " " (:sex %))}
  :scales {:facet {:domain titanic-panels}}
  :charts [(chart/bar {:position :stack})]
  :facets {:columns 4 :scales {:x :free}}
  :theme {:panel {:grid {:y :none}}}
  :labels {:x "Freq" :y nil}}
 {:width 900 :height 350})






21.2.11 Fig 2.11 Bars without borders
Source: Lattice Fig 2.11. Data: Titanic passengers and crew by class, sex, age and survival, R datasets package Titanic (Dawson 1995); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 {:data titanic
  :mapping {:x :n :y :class :color :survived :facet #(str (:age %) " " (:sex %))}
  :scales {:facet {:domain titanic-panels}}
  :charts [(chart/bar {:position :stack :stroke-color :none})]
  :facets {:columns 4 :scales {:x :free}}
  :theme {:panel {:grid {:x :none :y :none}}}
  :labels {:x "Freq" :y nil}}
 {:width 900 :height 350})

21.4 Chapter 4 - Displaying Multiway Tables

21.4.1 Fig 4.1 Dot plot of a table
Virginia death rates (1940) per 1000 by age group, a panel per population group.
Source: Lattice Fig 4.1. Data: Death rates in Virginia (1940), R datasets package VADeaths (Molyneaux et al. 1947); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 {:data va-deaths
  :mapping {:x :rate :y :age :facet :group}
  :charts [(chart/scatter)]
  :facets {:columns 2}
  :labels {:x "Freq" :y nil}}
 {:width 700 :height 450})






21.4.2 Fig 4.2 Stems from zero
Source: Lattice Fig 4.2. Data: Death rates in Virginia (1940), R datasets package VADeaths (Molyneaux et al. 1947); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 {:data va-deaths
  :mapping {:x :rate :y :age :facet :group}
  :charts [(chart/segment {:xend 0}) (chart/scatter)]
  :facets {:columns 1}
  :labels {:title "Death Rates in Virginia - 1940" :x "Rate (per 1000)" :y nil}}
 {:width 450 :height 750})






21.4.3 Fig 4.3 Groups joined
One line per population group across the age groups (the rows in age order, unsorted by rate).
Source: Lattice Fig 4.3. Data: Death rates in Virginia (1940), R datasets package VADeaths (Molyneaux et al. 1947); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 {:data (sort-by :age va-deaths)
  :mapping {:x :rate :y :age :color :group}
  :charts [(chart/line {:sort false}) (chart/scatter)]
  :labels {:title "Death Rates in Virginia - 1940" :x "Rate (per 1000)" :y nil}}
